ENTRY_FAILED paper:1910.01091 Error: Failed to parse. Text: "{
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "section_0",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "W-Net is a compact convolutional neural network research architecture for classifying five types of white blood cells in microscopy images."
            },
            {
              "type": "sourceCitation",
              "attrs": {
                "sourceChunkId": "f2765b26-100c-49d3-bc38-0cf9d621da33"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "section_1",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "“W-Net: A CNN-based Architecture for White Blood Cells Image Classification” asks whether a compact CNN can classify five white-blood-cell (WBC) types. The authors are Changhun Jung, Mohammed Abuhamad, Jumabek Alikhanov, Aziz Mohaisen, Kyungja Han and DaeHun Nyang. The reviewed evidence is an arXiv preprint, arXiv:1910.01091v1, dated 2 October 2019; formal venue publication is not established. The work reports average 97% accuracy on a private dataset and evaluates further training on LISC public data. No product or client-case relationship is established."
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " Read the "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "arXiv record",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.01091",
                        "target": "_blank"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " or "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "PDF",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1910.01091",
                        "target": "_blank"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                },
                {
                  "type": "sourceCitation",
                  "attrs": {
                    "sourceChunkId": "8caa1489-16a1-4678-b652-dc928ffd761e"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "key": "section_2",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Manual blood-smear review is described as time-consuming and dependent on operator experience, while WBC classification remains challenging after cells are observed. The task is to distinguish neutrophils, eosinophils, basophils, lymphocytes and monocytes; the study also addresses class imbalance. Its stated objective is classification, not leukemia diagnosis or a breast-cancer biomarker result."
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "sourceCitation",
                      "attrs": {
                        "sourceChunkId": "56469adb-4e9f-4aa2-ac35-137833b24a1c"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "sourceCitation",
                      "attrs": {
                        "sourceChunkId": "8caa1489-16a1-4678-b652-dc928ffd761e"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "key": "section_3",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The reported pipeline crops, resizes and normalizes cell images, then uses three convolutional layers with pooling to extract features. Two fully connected layers classify the image into five classes, with a softmax output. The authors describe the architecture as having a small number of layers; the model contains 16,806,949 trainable parameters."
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "sourceCitation",
                          "attrs": {
                            "sourceChunkId": "f2765b26-100c-49d3-bc38-0cf9d621da33"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "sourceCitation",
                          "attrs": {
                            "sourceChunkId": "505dca26-9178-4647-bb76-52645ec6ea1c"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "sourceCitation",
                          "attrs": {
                            "sourceChunkId": "423dfd02-49f0-4dba-8593-2004c685f142"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "key": "section_4",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "For the primary experiment, the team used 6,562 real RGB images supplied by The Catholic University of Korea, captured with a Sysmex DI60; the paper reports IRB approval. The five classes are represented in unequal numbers. Training used softmax loss, Adam with learning rate 0.0001, batch size 5 and 500 epochs, with 10-fold cross-validation. The paper also reports making the trained model available on GitHub, but this evidence does not establish a HumbleBeeAI product or production deployment."
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "sourceCitation",
                              "attrs": {
                                "sourceChunkId": "985bcc98-a886-4927-b0cc-dbc02640821c"
                              }
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "sourceCitation",
                              "attrs": {
                                "sourceChunkId": "423dfd02-49f0-4dba-8593-2004c685f142"
                              }
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "sourceCitation",
                              "attrs": {
                                "sourceChunkId": "f2765b26-100c-49d3-bc38-0cf9d621da33"
                              }
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "sourceCitation",
                              "attrs": {
                                "sourceChunkId": "0fd1d194-6ce7-45ac-9f56-5199fa414bcf"
                              }
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "key": "section_5",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "The reported primary result is average classification accuracy of 97% across five WBC classes on the private 6,562-image dataset, evaluated with 10-fold cross-validation. The authors say they compared W-Net with ResNet, but the supplied evidence does not provide the comparison’s numeric result or full test protocol."
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "sourceCitation",
                                  "attrs": {
                                    "sourceChunkId": "8caa1489-16a1-4678-b652-dc928ffd761e"
                                  }
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "sourceCitation",
                                  "attrs": {
                                    "sourceChunkId": "f2765b26-100c-49d3-bc38-0cf9d621da33"
                                  }
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "key": "section_6",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "paragraph",
                                  "content": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "text",
                                      "text": "On LISC public data, the study used 254 images and 10-fold cross-validation. Training a W-Net from scratch yielded 91% average accuracy; initializing with the model trained on the private data and then further training on LISC yielded 96%. Both models used 128×128×3 images and the same normalization, hardware environment and other stated hyperparameters; the training epoch counts differed. These are research measurements, not client or business outcomes."
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "type": "sourceCitation",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "sourceChunkId": "0fd1d194-6ce7-45ac-9f56-5199fa414bcf"
                                      }
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "type": "sourceCitation",
                                      "attrs": {
                                        "sourceChunkId": "0dfc3600-25ea-497f-885c-1eadb1f7da7c"
                                      }
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "key": "section_7",
                                  "content": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "paragraph",
                                      "content": [
                                        {
                                          "type": "text",
                                          "text": "The evidence does not specify hardware details, confidence intervals, independent external validation or clinical performance. The private dataset limits independent reproduction from the information provided. Although the paper discusses transfer learning, no future product work or next-step plan is established in the supplied records; publication approval and HumbleBeeAI review remain pending."
                                        },
                                        {
                                          "type": "sourceCitation",
                                          "attrs": {
                                            "sourceChunkId": "985bcc98-a886-4927-b0cc-dbc02640821c"
                                          }
                                        },
                                        {
                                          "type": "sourceCitation",
                                          "attrs": {
                                            "sourceChunkId": "0fd1d194-6ce7-45ac-9f56-5199fa414bcf"
                                          }
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "key": "section_8",
                                      "content": [
                                        {
                                          "type": "paragraph",
                                          "content": [
                                            {
                                              "type": "text",
                                              "text": "W-Net presents a compact CNN approach to five-class WBC image classification, reporting 97% average accuracy on a private dataset and improved LISC accuracy with further training. These findings support a research contribution only; they do not establish a deployed product, diagnostic result or measured business impact."
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "sourceCitation",
                                              "attrs": {
                                                "sourceChunkId": "8caa1489-16a1-4678-b652-dc928ffd761e"
                                              }
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "sourceCitation",
                                              "attrs": {
                                                "sourceChunkId": "0fd1d194-6ce7-45ac-9f56-5199fa414bcf"
                                              }
                                            }
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ],
                              "commentary": " "
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
